==> What is a Query in SQL?
A query in SQL (Structured Query Language) is a command used to communicate with a database.
It allows you to retrieve, insert, update, or delete data stored in database tables.

==> In simple words ->
An SQL query is a request given to a database to perform a specific operation on the data.

Example ->
SELECT * FROM students;
This query asks the database to retrieve all records from the students table.